What this solution actually does: it is the outbound leg of the SWIFT MT300 (FX confirmation) feed into Calypso. On every timer tick it marks the start of the tick in TOMI, reads the TOMI system date and ten system parameters (CALYPSO_MQ_*, CALYPSO_MT300_MAX_REGISTROS), refuses to run on a non-business day (raising an alert) or outside the configured CALYPSO_MQ_HORA_INICIO/CALYPSO_MQ_HORA_FIN window, and then calls sp_CinMT300_GetOperacionesMT300. That procedure scans the last eight days of TB_SRV_SWF_TRABAJO for incoming SWIFT MT-300 messages that have not been authorised or sent (NF_MQ_MSG_ETL IS NULL) and whose work-plan item is not yet PROC, extracts the trade date from the :30T: tag, marks the work-plan item `PROC` and the job row `NF_IMPRESION = '1'` for every candidate, and returns Folio, Mensaje, fechaTrade (all rows, or the first @MaxRegistros when it is greater than zero). The service then opens one ActiveMQ connection, publishes each message as a persistent text message to the CALYPSO_MQ_IN_MT300 queue and, after each publish, calls usp_CinMT300_UpdMT300Procesado, which stamps NF_HORA_AUTORIZACION, OFS_AUTHOR and NF_MQ_MSG_ETL = 'EXITOSO' on the job row. Any exception while sending or marking is logged, the rest of the batch is abandoned, and the connection is closed. The service does not consume from any queue, does not talk to T24 and moves no money; what Calypso does with the message, and who else reads NF_MQ_MSG_ETL/NF_IMPRESION, is not in this repository.
