3. What's Already Good
• Layering and seams. Aplicacion -> Infraestructura -> host with an interface for every collaborator (IMQServicio, IOperacionesTomi, IValidadorEjecucion, IAppLogger, IOperacionServicio), all constructor-injected (OperacionServicio.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_inMT300/Aplicacion_inMT300/OperacionServicio.cs):30-39). The business flow is therefore unit-testable without a broker or a database.
• Composition root. SimpleInjector with Verify() at start-up (ServiceHost.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_inMT300/Calypso_inMT300/ServiceHost.cs):91) and one scope per tick (:124-128); the MQ client is scoped to the tick, so a stale connection cannot be reused across ticks; overlapping ticks are prevented by the shared _tickLock in WindowsServiceHostBase.cs:372.
• Data access. Stored procedures with typed parameters only, no SQL text built in C#; the update path does the right thing with Exito and throws with the folio in the message (OperacionesTomiDao.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_inMT300/Infraestructura_inMT300/Repositorios/OperacionesTomiDao.cs):69-72). Both procedures use TRY/CATCH, write to Auditoria.ErrorLog and re-THROW; the update procedure sets SET XACT_ABORT ON.
• Exception hygiene. Every re-raise uses throw; (MQServicio.cs (../../CALYPSO/Calypso_inMT300/Infraestructura_inMT300/MQ/MQServicio.cs):61-76, OperacionesTomiDao.cs:47, 78); the connect path catches the specific NMS exception types and maps them to actionable text (MapConnectionError.cs).
• Messaging basics. Persistent delivery mode (MQServicio.cs:96), finally closing the connection on the send loop (OperacionServicio.cs:153-157), cancellation checked before every message (:139).
• Secrets. No credential in source, config or tests; CALYPSO_MQ_USER/CALYPSO_MQ_PSW are read from the parameter table and the shared FileLogger masks both keys by name when the parameter loader logs Parámetro 'CALYPSO_MQ_PSW' = '...' (FileLogger.cs:59, EnmascararPorClavesSensibles), so the password is not written to the log even though the request does not declare it sensitive (CMT-FR-20).
• Version-controlled database objects. Both procedures named by the constants exist under StoredProcedures\MWD_DB\DBMDW\CALYPSO\Calypso_inMT300\IT24\Procedures with headers, change control and matching parameter lists (@MaxRegistros; @Usuario, @Folio, @FechaOperacion), so the GEN-13 mismatch does not occur here.
• Start-up contract. ValidarContratoInicializacion (shared base) rejects a missing PID/process name before the timer starts, so the unguarded Pid.Value in the host fails loudly rather than silently.
• Hygiene. Compact solution (24 C# files, 1,408 lines), XML documentation on every public type, no Console/Debug output, build output git-ignored, a test project that targets the same framework and uses Moq.
