Issue: a procedure whose name says "Get" changes state. For every row of the eight-day window it flips the work-plan item to PROC and sets NF_IMPRESION = '1' *inside the loop*, before the service has published anything, and the NOT IN (... 'PROC') filter then hides those rows from every later call. The only thing that would make a row eligible again is NF_MQ_MSG_ETL IS NULL, but the next read excludes it through the PROC test. Therefore, whenever the work-plan row exists (the SP header says it is updated, so this is the normal case - *verify against data*):
1. `@MaxRegistros` drops the rest. TOP (@MaxRegistros) is applied only to the final SELECT; all other candidates were already marked PROC. The committed script sets CALYPSO_MT300_MAX_REGISTROS = '5' for the "controlled test"; with that value in any environment that has more than five candidates, every message beyond the fifth is marked processed and never sent. The parameter is read with a silent default (CMT-FR-9), so nothing warns that it is still set.
2. Any failure after the read loses the message. If the broker is down (ConectarAsync throws), the send throws, the process is stopped, or the host crashes, the rows are already PROC. The service only logs Validar manualmente (OperacionServicio.cs:150); there is no retry, no alert and no queue of "claimed but unsent" rows.
3. Operators may lose sight of the item. The work-plan row appears to be the manual work queue (inferred from its name and from the cve_usuario_realizar = 'TOMI' assignment); marking it PROC with fec_fin = GETDATE() makes an unsent confirmation look completed.
The C# code assumes the opposite contract (read = harmless, mark after send), which is why its comments and log messages talk about "actualizar manualmente".
Fix (claim/confirm, minimal version): make the read a pure read and move the state change to the confirmation, so a failure leaves the row eligible:
Code block (sql)
-- sp_CinMT300_GetOperacionesMT300: SELECT TOP (NULLIF(@MaxRegistros, 0)) ... ORDER BY NF_FECHA_INICIO, NF_FOLIO;  -- no UPDATE
-- usp_CinMT300_UpdMT300Procesado (one transaction, XACT_ABORT ON):
UPDATE tb_srv_swf_plan_trabajo_maestro SET cve_estatus = 'PROC', ... WHERE folio = @Folio ...;
UPDATE TB_SRV_SWF_TRABAJO SET NF_IMPRESION = '1', NF_HORA_AUTORIZACION = GETDATE(), OFS_AUTHOR = @Usuario,
                              NF_MQ_MSG_ETL = 'EXITOSO' WHERE NF_FOLIO = @Folio ...;
IF @@ROWCOUNT <> 1 THROW 50001, 'MT300 row not updated', 1;
Because a failed mark after a successful publish would then re-send the message, set NMSCorrelationID/a message property to the folio and agree an idempotency rule with the Calypso owners (CMT-FR-16); if a stronger guarantee is needed use a SENDING claim with a timestamp that a sweeper returns to INI and alerts on (see GEN-18).
Benefit: a stop, a broker outage or a send failure leaves confirmations pending instead of silently completed; @MaxRegistros becomes a real batch size. Suggested JIRA: CMT-1 (Blocker)
