Issue: the service passes registro.fechaTrade (the :30T: trade date, per the procedure header) as @FechaOperacion, and the update compares it with NF_FECHA_INICIO, the date the job row was created. Inside the read procedure the maestro update correctly uses the cursor's NF_FECHA_INICIO (@FECHA, :196), so the two procedures disagree about which date identifies a row. When a confirmation is created on a different day than its trade date (it arrives after midnight, after a weekend, or the deal is back-dated), the UPDATE matches zero rows. There is no @@ROWCOUNT check, the shared runner reports Exito, and the service logs "procesado correctamente" (OperacionServicio.cs:146). NF_MQ_MSG_ETL, NF_HORA_AUTORIZACION and OFS_AUTHOR stay NULL, so the audit trail says the message was never sent, and - depending on the CMT-FR-1 precondition - the message is either never marked (and may be re-sent every tick for up to eight days) or marked only in the work-plan table. Also, @Existe2 - 3 assumes a two-character line break after the date; a one-character break leaves a control character in @queFecha, and RTRIM removes only spaces. *Verify* with real data whether :30T: equals NF_FECHA_INICIO.
