CMT-FR-4 - Procedure hygiene: row-by-row cursor, dead string builder, reserved prefix, deprecated types (Minor) File: 001 SP (../../StoredProcedures/MWD_DB/DBMDW/CALYPSO/Calypso_inMT300/IT24/Procedures/001%20SP%20sp_CinMT300_GetOperacionesMT300.sql):11, 62, 93, 97-205, 109-123, 141-173, 210-225.
• Dead code. @Salida is assembled from {1:F01...}{2:O300...}{3:...}{4: (:141-152) and then overwritten by SET @Salida = @Mensaje; (:173, "Se conserva la lógica histórica"), and @Existe, @ExisteAnt and @Paso1 are declared and never used.
• `TOP` without `ORDER BY` on #salida (:212): which rows a limited run returns is arbitrary.
• Window and ordering. NF_FECHA_INICIO BETWEEN GETDATE() - 8 AND GETDATE() compares VARCHAR renderings and silently ignores any pending message older than eight days (for example after a long outage); ORDER BY NF_FECHA_INICIO DESC orders by the string alias, newest first, so older messages are starved when @MaxRegistros is set. Use ASC on the real datetime plus the folio as tie-breaker, and alert on rows that fall out of the window.
• `NOT IN (subquery)` returns no rows at all if the subquery ever yields a NULL folio; use NOT EXISTS.
• Row-by-row cursor plus a temp table with a deprecated TEXT column where a single set-based SELECT with TOP and one UPDATE ... OUTPUT would do.
• Naming. The sp_ prefix makes SQL Server look in master first and is reserved by Microsoft guidance; the sibling uses usp_. The header says SISTEMA/BD: TOMI while the script targets [InterfacesT24] (confirm both are the same database).
Fix: fold into the CMT-FR-1/2 rewrite; rename with usp_ and update ConstantesServicio.uspMT300Pendientes in the same release. Benefit: smaller, deterministic procedure that is cheaper to review and to test. Suggested JIRA: CMT-4 (Minor)
