Issue: MUFG_T24, Apache.NMS, Apache.NMS.ActiveMQ and SimpleInjector are taken from a drive-mapped folder with SpecificVersion=False, so the version compiled is whatever sits in that folder on that machine. packages.config in the Infraestructura and host projects restores Apache.NMS and Apache.NMS.ActiveMQ 2.2.0 (and SharpZipLib 1.3.3, which *is* referenced from ..\packages), but the NMS HintPaths point at D:\ServiceCMS, so the restored packages are not what is compiled; SimpleInjector is not restored at all. D:\ServiceCMS does not exist on the audit machine, no nuget.config exists, and the solution maps Debug|Any CPU to the x86 platform while MUFG_T24 is declared x86 (GEN-1). The empty PruebasUnitarias\bin\ and the restore-only obj\ are consistent with a build that could not finish.
Fix: publish MUFG_T24 as a versioned internal package and reference NMS and SimpleInjector through PackageReference with pinned versions; build in CI on a clean agent; remove the unused packages.config entries or make them the only source. Benefit: reproducible builds and a known runtime version; a prerequisite for CI and for the test project (CMT-FR-22). Suggested JIRA: CMT-19 (Blocker)
